{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"assumptions_and_dependencies\":\"The candidate assumes `FormalConjecturesUtil` exposes `omega`, `norm_num`, and `interval_cases`, and that Mathlib simplifies explicit `Finset.Icc` sums as expected. These assumptions could not be tested because no Lean toolchain executable is mounted.\",\"build_or_check_outcome\":\"Repository, hash, duplicate-search, and Python certificate commands succeeded. No Lean elaboration, kernel check, or project build was performed: `lake` was unavailable (`/bin/bash: line 1: lake: command not found`), and `lean`, `lake`, and `elan` were absent from PATH.\",\"case_id\":\"FIVE-01\",\"evidence\":\"FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/359.lean: declaration `Erdos359.erdos_359.variants.isGoodFor_1_low_values` found only at lines 55–57; its body is `by sorry`.\\n`git rev-parse HEAD` -> `9cbe1d3c12998c786b7c2cd99ce28a21b6631f66`.\\n`git hash-object FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/359.lean` -> `62635546c38f181610242b83e1e5d5ca86b5d64a`.\\n`sha256sum FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/359.lean` -> `184ece2c4fb5e0d29e72210c9d75573b93ba3ccc4b559619e1f3b4319ea20f61`.\\n`rg -n -uuu --glob '!.git/**'` and `git grep -n -E` for the declaration, exact set literal, compact sequence, `Erdos359`, and `IsGoodFor A 1` -> no proof or duplicate low-value result elsewhere; distinctive sequence occurs only in the target docstring and statement.\\n`git ls-files | wc -l` -> `1462`; `git status --porcelain=v1 | wc -l` -> `0` before and after checks.\\n`python3` finite recurrence check -> `[1, 2, 4, 5, 8, 10, 14, 15]`; successive least missing values -> `2,4,5,8,10,14,15`.\\n`lake env lean --version && lake --version` -> shell observation `/bin/bash: line 1: lake: command not found`; `command -v lean/lake/elan` produced no paths.\",\"limitations\":\"This is an unchecked Lean proof candidate, not a checked proof or acceptance claim. The Python computation confirms only the finite arithmetic certificate, not that the Lean term elaborates. The mounted source was not modified. No network or external authority was used.\",\"proposed_result\":\"Unchecked replacement for the target's `by sorry`:\\n\\nby\\n  rcases hA with ⟨h0, hmono, hleast⟩\\n  have upper (j c : ℕ) (hc : 0 < c) (hAj : A j < c)\\n      (hnone : ∀ a ≤ j, ∀ b ≤ j,\\n        c ≠ ∑ i ∈ Finset.Icc a b, A i) : A (j + 1) ≤ c := by\\n    apply (hleast j).2\\n    refine ⟨hAj, ?_⟩\\n    intro a b hab\\n    by_cases hba : a ≤ b\\n    · have ha : a ≤ j := by\\n        have ha' := hab (show a ∈ Finset.Icc a b by simp [hba])\\n        simpa using ha'\\n      have hb : b ≤ j := by\\n        have hb' := hab (show b ∈ Finset.Icc a b by simp [hba])\\n        simpa using hb'\\n      exact hnone a ha b hb\\n    · have hba' : b < a := by omega\\n      simpa [Finset.Icc_eq_empty_of_lt hba'] using Nat.ne_of_gt hc\\n  have notSum (j a b : ℕ) (hsub : Finset.Icc a b ⊆ Finset.Iic j) :\\n      A (j + 1) ≠ ∑ i ∈ Finset.Icc a b, A i :=\\n    (hleast j).1.2 a b hsub\\n  have h1 : A 1 = 2 := by\\n    have hu := upper 0 2 (by omega) (by omega) (by\\n      intro a ha b hb\\n      interval_cases a <;> interval_cases b <;> norm_num [h0])\\n    have hl := hmono (show 0 < 1 by omega)\\n    omega\\n  have h2 : A 2 = 4 := by\\n    have hu := upper 1 4 (by omega) (by omega) (by\\n      intro a ha b hb\\n      interval_cases a <;> interval_cases b <;> norm_num [h0, h1])\\n    have hn3 : A 2 ≠ 3 := by\\n      simpa [h0, h1] using notSum 1 0 1 (by simp)\\n    have hl := hmono (show 1 < 2 by omega)\\n    omega\\n  have h3 : A 3 = 5 := by\\n    have hu := upper 2 5 (by omega) (by omega) (by\\n      intro a ha b hb\\n      interval_cases a <;> interval_cases b <;> norm_num [h0, h1, h2])\\n    have hl := hmono (show 2 < 3 by omega)\\n    omega\\n  have h4 : A 4 = 8 := by\\n    have hu := upper 3 8 (by omega) (by omega) (by\\n      intro a ha b hb\\n      interval_cases a <;> interval_cases b <;> norm_num [h0, h1, h2, h3])\\n    have hn6 : A 4 ≠ 6